# 24-bit color for terminals that accept only the legacy semicolon form of the
# SGR truecolor sequence. ncurses' stock xterm-direct emits the ITU-T T.416
# colon form (\E[38:2::R:G:Bm); Windows Terminal drops it silently, which takes
# every color with it. Same capability, ";" separators and no colorspace field.
xterm-direct-wt|xterm-direct with semicolon-separated 24-bit SGR,
	setab=\E[%?%p1%{8}%<%t4%p1%d%e48;2;%p1%{65536}%/%d;%p1%{256}%/%{255}%&%d;%p1%{255}%&%d%;m,
	setaf=\E[%?%p1%{8}%<%t3%p1%d%e38;2;%p1%{65536}%/%d;%p1%{256}%/%{255}%&%d;%p1%{255}%&%d%;m,
	use=xterm-direct,

tmux-direct-wt|tmux-direct with semicolon-separated 24-bit SGR,
	setab=\E[%?%p1%{8}%<%t4%p1%d%e48;2;%p1%{65536}%/%d;%p1%{256}%/%{255}%&%d;%p1%{255}%&%d%;m,
	setaf=\E[%?%p1%{8}%<%t3%p1%d%e38;2;%p1%{65536}%/%d;%p1%{256}%/%{255}%&%d;%p1%{255}%&%d%;m,
	use=tmux-direct,
